		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4992&amp;p=36556#p36556"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Only a proposal for GD-77S improvement<br><br>Hello,<br><br>recently I got a GD-77S. I flashed OpenGD77 firmware and prepared a seperate codeplug. Thank you very much for the implementation of OpenGD77 firmware! Very amazing... But I found it was hard to program because there is no TG-list available. So all frequencies have to be programmed with an individual talkgroup (like the chinese firmware/CPSs). With adding a TG-list as an extra control menu you could choose a frequency within a zone and after selecting the TG-list menu you could step through the TGs with the rotary switch. That would be similar to the devices with a display and would be very helpful on all DMR repeater frequencies. Perhaps that could be implemented somewhere in the future if time allows it.<br><br>Thank you very much again for your excellent work!<br>73s de DF1OG, Ingo</div></blockquote><br>You have TG-List support.<br>Select the "Contacts" menu, and select le contact you want to use.<br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#gd-77s-operation" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... -operation</a><br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Apr 01, 2025 8:57 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
